# Squeezelite runtime configuration
# Edit this file on the running device (e.g. over SSH) — no rebuild required.
#
# SL_OPTIONS is passed directly to squeezelite. Common flags:
#   -n <name>   Player name shown in LMS            (default: hostname)
#   -s <addr>   LMS server IP or hostname           (default: mDNS auto-discovery)
#   -o <dev>    ALSA output device                  (default: default)
#   -a <b>:<p>  Buffer size:period count
#
# Examples:
#   SL_OPTIONS="-n LivingRoom"
#   SL_OPTIONS="-n LivingRoom -s 192.168.1.10"
#
# With no -s flag squeezelite discovers LMS automatically via mDNS,
# which requires avahi-daemon to be running (already included in this image).

SL_OPTIONS="-n raspberrypi"
